WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.880
Test 3. This is the IELTS listening test. You will hear a number of different recordings

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:14.760
and you will have to answer questions on what you hear. There will be time for you to read

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:21.280
the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work. All the

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:29.680
recordings will be played once only. The test is in four parts. At the end of the test you

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:36.480
will be given 10 minutes to transfer your answers to an answer sheet.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:47.680
Now turn to part 1. Part 1. You will hear a woman phoning the owner

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:54.720
of a house she is going to rent about companies that she could rent furniture from. First

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.119
you have some time to look at questions 1 to 5.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:32.720
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 5.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:42.720
Good morning. Hi, this is Shelley Meyer. I'm renting your house on Archwood Avenue. I'm

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.720
due to move in next week. Oh yes, hello Ms. Meyer. What can I do for

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:50.720
you? When I viewed the house I told you I'll most

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.720
probably need to rent some furniture, at least until I know whether my temporary work

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:01.720
contract is going to be made permanent. Yes, of course, I remember. And I said I could

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.720
give you some information about furniture rental companies in the city.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:10.720
That's right. Well, the biggest company is called Peak Rentals.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.720
I've recommended them to other people and have always heard positive reports about them.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:21.720
Could you give me an idea of their costs? Sure. I actually have one of their brochures

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:31.720
here. It says the monthly price per room starts at $105 and goes up to $239. That depends

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.720
on which rooms you need furniture for, of course.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:41.720
Sure. It's just to get a general idea of how much it's going to cost. And you said you

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:47.720
had some positive feedback about this company? Yes. People have mentioned that the furniture

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:53.720
from Peak Rentals is more modern than any of the other companies. And also, once you

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:58.720
place an order, the furniture will be delivered to you in just one or two days.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:04.720
That would be really helpful. Oh, and the brochure says that there's a

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:10.720
special offer at the moment. If you rent living room furniture, I believe that's a set of

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.720
chairs and a TV table. You'll also get a lamp at no extra cost.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:22.720
Okay, but you know, that price range you gave is more than I was hoping to pay.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.720
Then you could try Aaron and Oliver. Sorry, what and Oliver?

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.720
Aaron. Double A-R-O-N. Okay. Are they cheaper?

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.720
I'd say they're a mid-price company. But if you chose them, you need to be aware that

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.720
they charge an extra 12% every month in case of damage.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:49.720
Oh, I see. I'd have to do the math carefully then.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.720
Right. But one helpful thing is that they also do cleaning for customers.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.720
For the furniture? For the house.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.720
Oh, I see. I probably won't need that.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:07.720
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 6 to 10.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:49.720
Now listen and answer questions 6 to 10.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:58.720
There's another company called Larch Furniture. It's quite new and it has the lowest prices

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.720
in town. That's for both furniture and also electronic equipment.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:09.720
Well, that would be good. I'm not bringing much with me and I won't have much time to

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.720
go shopping after I start my job.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.720
There are two things you need to know about Larch Furniture.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.720
First of all, you have to take out insurance on the furniture and you need to organize

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:22.720
that yourself.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.720
That wouldn't be too hard.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:31.720
Also, you can't take out a contract for less than six months, but I figure that might not

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:36.720
be a problem for you. You're renting the house for twelve months after all, aren't you?

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:45.720
Sorry to interrupt. I just thought of another furniture rental company. It's called Space

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.720
Rentals and it's located very near to the house.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:56.720
I don't have any information about their charges, so it's best to use their app to find out

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.720
what it would cost you to use them.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:05.720
One good thing about that company is that if you don't like the furniture once it's

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:10.720
delivered, you can request exchanges, as long as you do that within a week of receiving

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:11.720
it.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:28.720
That is the end of Part 1. You now have one minute to check your answers to Part 1.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:50.720
Thank you.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:21.720
Thank you.

